{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LYMwG5rE8CNFDETgMSfwXc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu OAuth scopes ACTIVITY:READ WELLNESS:READ CALENDAR:WRITE authorize\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu OAuth support\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759\"},{\"title\":\"Überauth intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0\"},{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090\"},{\"title\":\"← All articles\",\"url\":\"https://www.athletedata.health/guides/intervals-icu-mcp-server\"},{\"title\":\"intervals icu tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\"},{\"title\":\"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io\",\"url\":\"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/latest/autoapi/intervalsicu/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io\",\"url\":\"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/docs/autoapi/intervalsicu/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"intervals wellness\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/freekode/intervals-wellness\"},{\"title\":\"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io\",\"url\":\"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/docs/autoapi/intervalsicu/api/intervals/index.html\"}]\n\nThe main source is the official intervals.icu OAuth thread, which documents the scope format but doesn't confirm that this exact three-scope combination is valid.\n\n- **Authorize URL:** The app sends the user to the intervals.icu `/oauth/authorize` endpoint with a client ID, redirect URI, a `scope` parameter, and optional state. Intervals.icu will ask the user to login and display a confirmation dialog with options to choose which scopes to grant the application.\n- **Scope syntax:** The thread lists ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, CALENDAR, CHATS, LIBRARY, and SETTINGS as scopes. Each needs READ or WRITE, with commas between them. CALENDAR covers planned workouts. For each scope specify READ or WRITE (to update, implies READ access) and use commas to separate multiple scopes. So a request would look like `ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`, with commas and no spaces.\n- **Token exchange:** If the user approves, the app gets a code that must be exchanged within 2 minutes. If all goes well Intervals.icu will respond with an access token, granted scopes and the id and name of the athlete.\n- **Related wellness write scope:** A different community cookbook says updating wellness data requires the WELLNESS:WRITE scope for the bulk wellness endpoint. That matters if you plan to write wellness data, since READ alone won't allow it.\n- **Redirect URIs:** A community Elixir library notes that intervals.icu does not support wildcards in redirect URIs, so each callback URL has to be registered in full.\n\nI didn't find a source that confirms the exact combination `ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` is accepted in a live authorize request, or describes the consent screen's wording. Check that against the live app or the official thread.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0fb6539-8306-4def-bc57-954b92d4e42c","uuid":"22b35256-a5ae-4195-9e5c-3f1556f47796","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:24:13.194Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu OAuth scopes ACTIVITY:READ WELLNESS:READ CALENDAR:WRITE authorize","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FW4tEAcCpaX82XuLda3heJ","content":[{"title":"Intervals.icu OAuth support","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759"},{"title":"Überauth intervals.icu","url":"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0"},{"title":"Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090"},{"title":"← All articles","url":"https://www.athletedata.health/guides/intervals-icu-mcp-server"},{"title":"intervals icu tools","url":"https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools"},{"title":"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io","url":"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/latest/autoapi/intervalsicu/index.html"},{"title":"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io","url":"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/docs/autoapi/intervalsicu/index.html"},{"title":"intervals wellness","url":"https://github.com/freekode/intervals-wellness"},{"title":"py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io","url":"https://py-intervalsicu.readthedocs.io/en/docs/autoapi/intervalsicu/api/intervals/index.html"}]},"The main source is the official intervals.icu OAuth thread, which documents the scope format but doesn't confirm that this exact three-scope combination is valid.\n\n- **Authorize URL:** The app sends the user to the intervals.icu `/oauth/authorize` endpoint with a client ID, redirect URI, a `scope` parameter, and optional state. Intervals.icu will ask the user to login and display a confirmation dialog with options to choose which scopes to grant the application.\n- **Scope syntax:** The thread lists ACTIVITY, WELLNESS, CALENDAR, CHATS, LIBRARY, and SETTINGS as scopes. Each needs READ or WRITE, with commas between them. CALENDAR covers planned workouts. For each scope specify READ or WRITE (to update, implies READ access) and use commas to separate multiple scopes. So a request would look like `ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`, with commas and no spaces.\n- **Token exchange:** If the user approves, the app gets a code that must be exchanged within 2 minutes. If all goes well Intervals.icu will respond with an access token, granted scopes and the id and name of the athlete.\n- **Related wellness write scope:** A different community cookbook says updating wellness data requires the WELLNESS:WRITE scope for the bulk wellness endpoint. That matters if you plan to write wellness data, since READ alone won't allow it.\n- **Redirect URIs:** A community Elixir library notes that intervals.icu does not support wildcards in redirect URIs, so each callback URL has to be registered in full.\n\nI didn't find a source that confirms the exact combination `ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` is accepted in a live authorize request, or describes the consent screen's wording. Check that against the live app or the official thread."],"durationSeconds":6.645327874999999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LYMwG5rE8CNFDETgMSfwXc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
